    "explanation": "FileVault scrambles everything on your disk so it can only be read with your password. Without it, anyone who takes the Mac, or just its drive, can read your files by plugging it into another computer. It is the single most important setting on a laptop that ever leaves the house.",
    "fix": {
      "apply": {
        "kind": "deep_link",
        "pane": "filevault",
        "reveal": null,
        "watch": [
          "diskEncryption",
        ],
        "watchEvery": 3,
